course: dictionary
lesson: 9560
title: The stove
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A stove is a thing you cook on or use to heat a room. «Never leave the stove on when nobody is watching it.» The sentence tells you the stove gets hot and makes heat, so it must be something you cook on, not something you wash or sleep on.
explain: The meaning can change with the words around it. «Grandma lit the wood stove to warm the room.» Here the stove is a closed metal box that burns wood to heat the room. A stove in a kitchen cooks food, while a stove in a living room warms the air.
explain: Other words in a text give clues too. «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent, because of fire and carbon monoxide, a poison gas you cannot smell.» The warning about fire tells you a stove is a heat source, and it must never be used inside a tent.
fact: A stove is a piece of kitchen equipment for cooking, with hot rings or burners on top and often an oven.
fact: A stove can also be a closed metal box that burns wood, coal or gas to heat a room.
fact: Stove is a noun. One stove, two stoves.
fact: In British English a stove is often called a cooker or a hob.
fact: Phrases you may meet are on the stove, stovetop, gas stove, wood stove and camping stove.
exercise: «Never leave the stove on when nobody is watching it.» What is a stove? | *Kitchen equipment for cooking, with hot rings or burners on top | A small tent for camping | A wide metal tub for washing clothes | A cupboard for plates and cups
exercise: Grandma lit the wood stove to warm the room. What is its job here? | To cook eggs for breakfast only | *To heat a room by burning wood | To keep food cold | To wash clothes in a tub
exercise: Find and copy the one word that names a cooking device in this sentence: «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent.» | *stove | inside | tent | never
test: «The camping stove boiled water for tea on the hill.» Where would you use a camping stove? | *Outdoors | Under the bed | Inside a tent with the flaps closed | In a bathtub
test: Leo says a stove is the same as a fridge because both are in kitchens. Why is he wrong? | A fridge is a kind of stove | *A stove heats things to cook them, but a fridge keeps food cold | A stove is only used in bathrooms | A stove and a fridge both keep food cold
exam: Read «Clothes were pressed with heavy irons heated on the stove.» Which word is the best clue that a stove gives heat? | clothes | pressed | *heated | heavy
